sect3.example:
PHP 7.3.0 अनुसारको आधारभूत Heredoc उदाहरण
<?php // closing identifier मा indentation नराखिएको echo <<<END a b c \n END;
// closing identifier मा 3 spaces को indentation राखिएको; प्रत्येक line बाट 3 spaces हटाइन्छ echo <<<END a b c END;
&example.outputs.73;
a b c
a b c

Closing identifier लाई body का कुनै पनि line भन्दा बढी indent गर्नु हुँदैन
<?php echo <<<END a b c END;
&example.outputs.73;
Parse error: Invalid body indentation level (expecting an indentation level of at least 3) in example.php on line 4

    Body र closing identifier का लागि फरक indentation


<?php
// तलका कुनै पनि code ले काम गर्दैनन्।

// body (spaces) र ending marker (tabs) मा फरक indentation
{
	echo <<<END
	 a
		END;
}

// body मा spaces र tabs मिसाइएको
{
    echo <<<END
    	a
     END;
}

// ending marker मा spaces र tabs मिसाइएको
{
	echo <<<END
		  a
		 END;
}


    &example.outputs.73;


Parse error: Invalid indentation - tabs and spaces cannot be mixed in example.php line 8

Closing identifier पछि expression लाई निरन्तरता दिने
<?php $values = [<<<END a b c END, 'd e f']; var_dump($values);
&example.outputs.73;
array(2) { [0] => string(11) "a b c" [1] => string(5) "d e f" }

warning.example:
String को body मा closing identifier पर्दा ParseError आउन सक्छ
<?php $values = [<<<END a b END ING END, 'd e f'];
&example.outputs.73;
Parse error: syntax error, unexpected identifier "ING", expecting "]" in example.php on line 5

sect3.example:
    Heredoc string quoting उदाहरण


<?php
$str = <<<EOD
Example of string
spanning multiple lines
using heredoc syntax.
EOD;

/* Variables सहितको अलि जटिल उदाहरण। */
class foo
{
    var $foo;
    var $bar;

    function __construct()
    {
        $this->foo = 'Foo';
        $this->bar = array('Bar1', 'Bar2', 'Bar3');
    }
}

$foo = new foo();
$name = 'MyName';

echo <<<EOT
My name is "$name". I am printing some $foo->foo.
Now, I am printing some {$foo->bar[1]}.
This should print a capital 'A': \x41
EOT;
?>


    &example.outputs;


My name is "MyName". I am printing some Foo.
Now, I am printing some Bar2.
This should print a capital 'A': A

    Nowdoc string quoting उदाहरण


<?php
echo <<<'EOD'
Example of string spanning multiple lines
using nowdoc syntax. Backslashes are always treated literally,
e.g. \\ and \'.
EOD;


    &example.outputs;


Example of string spanning multiple lines
using nowdoc syntax. Backslashes are always treated literally,
e.g. \\ and \'.

    Variables सहितको Nowdoc string quoting उदाहरण


<?php
class foo
{
    public $foo;
    public $bar;

    function __construct()
    {
        $this->foo = 'Foo';
        $this->bar = array('Bar1', 'Bar2', 'Bar3');
    }
}

$foo = new foo();
$name = 'MyName';

echo <<<'EOT'
My name is "$name". I am printing some $foo->foo.
Now, I am printing some {$foo->bar[1]}.
This should not print a capital 'A': \x41
EOT;
?>


    &example.outputs;


My name is "$name". I am printing some $foo->foo.
Now, I am printing some {$foo->bar[1]}.
This should not print a capital 'A': \x41

sect4.example:
     String Interpolation


<?php
$juice = "apple";

echo "He drank some $juice juice." . PHP_EOL;

?>


     &example.outputs;


He drank some apple juice.

warning.para:
      PHP 8.2.0 देखि ${ expression } syntax लाई deprecated गरिएको छ, किनभने यसलाई variable variables को रूपमा अर्थ लगाउन सकिन्छ:



<?php
const foo = 'bar';
$foo = 'foo';
$bar = 'bar';
var_dump("${foo}");
var_dump("${(foo)}");
?>


       &example.outputs.82;


Deprecated: Using ${var} in strings is deprecated, use {$var} instead in file on line 6

Deprecated: Using ${expr} (variable variables) in strings is deprecated, use {${expr}} instead in file on line 9
string(3) "foo"
string(3) "bar"


       &example.outputs;


string(3) "foo"
string(3) "bar"



      यसको सट्टा advanced string interpolation syntax प्रयोग गर्नुपर्छ।

sect4.example:
     Array को पहिलो आयाम वा property को मान interpolate गर्ने


<?php
$juices = array("apple", "orange", "string_key" => "purple");

echo "He drank some $juices[0] juice.";
echo PHP_EOL;
echo "He drank some $juices[1] juice.";
echo PHP_EOL;
echo "He drank some $juices[string_key] juice.";
echo PHP_EOL;

class A {
    public $s = "string";
}

$o = new A();

echo "Object value: $o->s.";
?>


     &example.outputs;


He drank some apple juice.
He drank some orange juice.
He drank some purple juice.
Object value: string.

ऋणात्मक (Negative) numeric indices


<?php
$string = 'string';
echo "The character at index -2 is $string[-2].", PHP_EOL;
$string[-3] = 'o';
echo "Changing the character at index -3 to o gives $string.", PHP_EOL;
?>


     &example.outputs;


The character at index -2 is n.
Changing the character at index -3 to o gives strong.

sect3.example:
    अवैध (Illegal) String Offsets को उदाहरण


<?php
$str = 'abc';

$keys = [ '1', '1.0', 'x', '1x' ];

foreach ($keys as $keyToTry) {
    var_dump(isset($str[$keyToTry]));

    try {
        var_dump($str[$keyToTry]);
    } catch (TypeError $e) {
        echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
    }

    echo PHP_EOL;
}
?>


    &example.outputs.8;


bool(true)
string(1) "b"

bool(false)
Cannot access offset of type string on string

bool(false)
Cannot access offset of type string on string

bool(false)

Warning: Illegal string offset "1x" in example.php on line 10
string(1) "b"


    &example.outputs.7;


bool(true)
string(1) "b"

bool(false)

Warning: Illegal string offset '1.0' in example.php on line 10
string(1) "b"

bool(false)

Warning: Illegal string offset 'x' in example.php on line 10
string(1) "a"

bool(false)

Notice: A non well formed numeric value encountered in example.php on line 10
string(1) "b"
